# Records-audio AWS configuration for the backend Deployment.
#
# DO NOT copy this file into the cluster as-is — fill in real values and
# apply, or use `kubectl create secret generic ...` to skip the
# committed-placeholder problem.
#
# Credentials model in prod:
#
#   1. Bootstrap = IRSA. The pod's ServiceAccount is annotated with an
#      IAM role; EKS injects AWS_WEB_IDENTITY_TOKEN_FILE +
#      AWS_ROLE_ARN into the pod automatically. The SDK uses those to
#      call sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity for bootstrap credentials.
#      No static AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID / AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY in the
#      cluster; nothing in this file.
#
#   2. Records-audio writer role = AWS_ASSUME_ROLE_ARN. The backend
#      explicitly assumes this role on top of the bootstrap creds via
#      stscreds.AssumeRoleProvider. Permissions:
#        s3:PutObject, s3:GetObject, s3:HeadObject on
#          arn:aws:s3:::${AWS_S3_BUCKET}/${AWS_S3_KEY_PREFIX}users/*
#      and nothing else.
#
# CI is different (kind has no OIDC issuer for IRSA): the same secret
# also carries static AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID / AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY pointing
# at MinIO root, plus AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_S3 + AWS_S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=1
# to redirect the SDK off public AWS. AWS_ASSUME_ROLE_ARN is unset in
# CI (MinIO has no STS endpoint).
#
# The backend refuses to boot without AWS_REGION + AWS_S3_BUCKET in
# this secret. Other vars are optional from the boot validator's
# perspective, even though they may be operationally required (e.g.
# AWS_ASSUME_ROLE_ARN in prod).
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: aws-records-audio
type: Opaque
stringData:
  AWS_REGION: "ap-northeast-2"
  AWS_S3_BUCKET: "dear-baby-records-REPLACE_ENV"
  AWS_S3_KEY_PREFIX: "REPLACE_ENV/"
  AWS_ASSUME_ROLE_ARN: "arn:aws:iam::REPLACE_ACCOUNT_ID:role/dear-baby-records-writer"
